-- title:
--   Transport of pole-chart regularity along automorphisms fixing j
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero; an element $\zeta \in L$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity; a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = \exp(2\pi i/q)$; an intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq L(\!(X)\!)$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(X)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise image of that field of $q$-expansions over $\mathbb{Q}$; a discrete valuation domain $A$ with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$; an element $j \in K$, nonzero, whose Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the $j$-invariant under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81); an element $\varpi \in A$; and an $L$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $K$ with $\sigma j = j$. Write $B$ for `chartAlgInf A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. Let $Y$ be a prime ideal of $B$ such that every localisation $C$ of $B$ at $Y$ is a regular local ring and $C/(\varpi)$ is a regular local ring, and let $Y'$ be a prime ideal of $B$ whose elements $b'$ are exactly those with $b' = \sigma b$ in $K$ for some $b \in Y$. Then for any localisation $B_m$ of $B$ at $Y'$, $B_m$ is a regular local ring and so is $B_m/(\varpi)$, the quotient by the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$.
--
--   This is the transport-of-structure step for the integral model at the cusps: regularity of the pole chart (the integral closure of $A[1/j]$ in the function field) and of its special fibre at one prime propagates to every prime in the same orbit under the $L$-automorphisms of $K$ fixing $j$, i.e. under the Galois action on the cusps lying over $j = \infty$. It is used in the companion statement deducing regularity of the pole chart and its fibre at all primes of the cuspidal fibre.
